%% Trust triangle — signature, SLSA provenance and SBOM: where the trusted pipeline produces them and
%% where they are checked (Conforma in the pipeline, the policy controller at admission). Illustrates
%% concept.adoc "Policy as a gate, and policy as an admission control" and the demo Brief.
%% Layout: two direction-LR subgraphs stacked TB, joined container-to-container only (SRC-->PIPE,
%% PIPE-->ADMIT), so each `direction LR` is honoured (tools/lint/diagram-size-guard.py, ignored-direction).
%% 2026-11-15: redrawn for the one-pipeline design (Chains signs keyless; Conforma; admission webhook).
flowchart TB
  SRC[(Your fork<br/>parasol-claims)] --> PIPE
  subgraph PIPE["parasol-claims-trusted-build, in your -cicd project"]
    direction LR
    BUILD[build-image<br/>buildah] --> SCAN{scan<br/>RHACS}
    BUILD --> SBOM[sbom<br/>CycloneDX]
    BUILD -. Tekton Chains signs, keyless .-> SIG[[signature + SLSA provenance<br/>next to the image]]
    SCAN --> EC{verify-conforma<br/>Conforma}
    SBOM --> EC
    EC --> DEP([deploy<br/>by digest])
    SCAN -->|CVE found| STOP[/run fails —<br/>never deployed/]
  end
  subgraph ADMIT["admission — every pod in your -cicd project"]
    direction LR
    ADM{policy controller<br/>webhook} -->|Chains-signed| RUN([pod runs])
    ADM -->|anything else| DENY[/refused/]
  end
  PIPE -->|"any deploy"| ADMIT
  classDef g fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#137333,color:#0d652d;
  classDef r fill:#fce8e6,stroke:#c5221f,color:#a50e0e;
  class SIG,DEP,RUN g;
  class STOP,DENY r;
